# Quiver — Grouped Express Data

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Keep each group's positions and components together

`Plotly.quiver/2` accepts the same table inputs as the other Express helpers.
All four selectors are required. Interleaved groups below become separate
traces, with each group's `x`, `y`, `u`, and `v` arrays kept in row order.
List-of-map inputs use string keys. An Explorer DataFrame can be passed with
the same selectors.

```elixir
data = [
  %{"x" => 0, "y" => 0, "u" => 1, "v" => 0, "field" => "east"},
  %{"x" => 0, "y" => 1, "u" => 0, "v" => 1, "field" => "north"},
  %{"x" => 1, "y" => 0, "u" => 1, "v" => 0, "field" => "east"},
  %{"x" => 1, "y" => 1, "u" => 0, "v" => 1, "field" => "north"}
]

Plotly.quiver(data, x: "x", y: "y", u: "u", v: "v", color: "field")
|> Plotly.Figure.update_layout(
  title: "Two interleaved vector groups", yaxis: %{scaleanchor: "x"}
)
|> Plotly.show()
```
